          "python",
          "Without CoT: \"What is 47 x 83?\"\n-> Model might guess wrong\n\nWith CoT: \"What is 47 x 83? Think step by step.\"\n-> 47 x 80 = 3,760\n-> 47 x 3 = 141  \n-> 3,760 + 141 = 3,901\n-> Answer: 3,901"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "A company has 3 servers. Server A handles 40% of traffic with 2% error rate.\nServer B handles 35% with 5% error rate. Server C handles 25% with 1% error rate.\nWhat is the overall error rate?\n\nThink through this step by step:\n1. Server A contribution: 40% x 2% = 0.8%\n2. Server B contribution: 35% x 5% = 1.75%  \n3. Server C contribution: 25% x 1% = 0.25%\n4. Total: 0.8% + 1.75% + 0.25% = 2.8%\n\nAnswer: 2.8%"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "import collections\n\ndef solve_with_consistency(prompt, n=5):\n    '''Run the same CoT prompt multiple times, take majority answer.'''\n    answers = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        response = ask(prompt + \"\\nThink step by step.\", temperature=0.7)\n        answer = extract_final_answer(response)\n        answers.append(answer)\n    return collections.Counter(answers).most_common(1)[0][0]"
        ]
      ]
    }
